Package: reread
Type: Package
Title: Screening Careless Respondents with a Self-Calibrating Threshold
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Vittorio", "Guerrieri", email = "v.guerrieri4@campus.unimib.it",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Marcello", "Gallucci", role = "aut"),
    person("Marcello", "Passarelli", email = "passarelli@itd.cnr.it", role = "aut"))
Description: Screens questionnaire data for careless or insufficient-effort
    responding, and -- unlike index-only tools -- decides where to cut without
    labels. The threshold is anchored on the attentive mode of the score
    distribution, estimated from that mode's left flank alone, and is reported
    together with a calibrated prevalence estimate and with what the same rule
    flags on careless-free data of the same size. The score it cuts is 'rc'
    (relative coherence), a permutation-based index of individual response
    coherence that needs no declared factor structure, combined with two
    complementary detectors (longstring and person-total correlation) in a compact,
    profile-gated logistic ensemble with frozen weights; the same threshold can be
    applied to person-total alone. The package is a faithful port of the shipped
    browser tool and reproduces its scores. Utilities are provided for simulating
    careless responding and for benchmarking against the indices in the 'careless'
    package. Methods are described in Guerrieri, Gallucci, and Passarelli (2026).
